About WPP Media

WPP is the trusted growth partner for the world’s leading brands. With exceptional talent, trusted data and intelligence, and world-class partnerships - all united by our pioneering agentic marketing platform, WPP Open - we help clients navigate change, capture opportunity, and deliver transformational growth. 

WPP Media is WPP's AI-driven media operating unit, bringing together media, data, and partnerships to deliver creative personalisation at scale. Connected through WPP Open and powered by Open Intelligence, clients see exactly where, how, and why their media investment is working.

For more information, visit wppmedia.com .

Key Responsibilities &nbsp;

eCommerce Strategy &amp; Growth &nbsp;

• Lead and define overall eCommerce strategy across marketplaces (Shopee, TikTok Shop, and others) to drive revenue, profitability, and sustainable growth. &nbsp;

• Develop integrated approaches covering onsite performance, affiliates, creators, operations, and promotions. &nbsp;

• Identify&nbsp;growth opportunities through data-driven insights, platform innovations, and competitive benchmarking. &nbsp;

Marketplace &amp; Media Expertise &nbsp;

• Own in-app and&nbsp;onsite&nbsp;advertising strategies for Shopee and TikTok (e.g.&nbsp;search ads, discovery ads, live ads, product ads). &nbsp;

• Optimize&nbsp;performance through budget allocation, funnel strategy, and continuous testing. &nbsp;

• Stay up to date with platform algorithm changes, new ad products, and best practices. &nbsp;

Operations &amp; Affiliate Ecosystem &nbsp;

• Oversee end-to-end marketplace operations, including campaign planning, product readiness, pricing,&nbsp;logistics&nbsp;coordination, and execution. &nbsp;

• Lead affiliate and&nbsp;creator&nbsp;commerce strategies, ensuring alignment between content, traffic, and conversion. &nbsp;

• Collaborate closely with internal and external stakeholders to ensure seamless execution. &nbsp;

Team Leadership &amp; Management &nbsp;

• Lead, coach, and develop multi-functional eCommerce teams (media, affiliates, operations). &nbsp;

• Set clear KPIs, ensure accountability, and build a strong performance-driven culture. &nbsp;

• Act as a mentor and escalation point for complex commercial or operational challenges. &nbsp;

Client &amp; Stakeholder Management &nbsp;

• Serve as a senior client-facing representative in strategic meetings, reviews, and business planning sessions. &nbsp;

• Build trust and credibility with clients through strong marketplace knowledge and clear recommendations. &nbsp;

• Translate client business&nbsp;objectives&nbsp;into actionable eCommerce strategies. &nbsp;

Requirements &amp; Qualifications &nbsp;

• Strong background in eCommerce marketplaces, with hands-on experience across media, affiliates, and operations. &nbsp;

• Prior experience at&nbsp;eCommerce&nbsp;and/or leading beauty players. &nbsp;

• Proven&nbsp;track record&nbsp;managing and scaling eCommerce performance for brands or clients. &nbsp;

Skills &amp; Competencies &nbsp;

• Deep understanding of Shopee and TikTok Shop ecosystems, including in-app / onsite advertising. &nbsp;

• Strong leadership and people management capabilities. &nbsp;

• Commercial mindset with the ability to balance growth and efficiency. &nbsp;

• Confident communicator with experience leading client-facing discussions and presentations. &nbsp;

• Analytical, structured, and comfortable making decisions in a fast-paced environment. &nbsp;

• Ready to engage directly with senior stakeholders and clients. &nbsp;

• High ownership, adaptability, and collaborative mindset. &nbsp;

&nbsp;

About WPP Media &nbsp;

WPP Media is WPP’s global media collective, bringing together world-class media agencies, talent, and capabilities. We partner with clients to unlock growth by combining strategic thinking, creativity, and performance-driven media solutions. &nbsp;

At WPP Media, our people and culture are at the heart of everything we do.

This is Adyen

Adyen provides payments, data, and financial products in a single solution for customers like Meta, Uber, H&amp;M, and Microsoft - making us the financial technology platform of choice. At Adyen, everything we do is engineered for ambition.&nbsp;

For our teams, we create an environment with opportunities for our people to succeed, backed by the culture and support to ensure they are enabled to truly own their careers. We are motivated individuals who tackle unique technical challenges at scale and solve them as a team. Together, we deliver innovative and ethical solutions that help businesses achieve their ambitions faster.

About the role

Adyen is looking for a Group Financial Controller to join our Group Finance team in Amsterdam. This is a unique opportunity for someone looking to challenge the status quo, who gets truly excited to re-imagine processes from the ground up.&nbsp;

In this role, you will partner, validate and drive financial excellence across our global footprint. Rather than focusing on routine data production, you will have the mandate to redesign leverage automation and modern tooling to enable a continuous and low-touch close while maintaining a control environment.

At Adyen we like to build things ourselves - in this team you will play a key role in applying out-of-the box solutions to improve control and streamline ways of working.

What you’ll do

• Partner with FinOps and Financial Data Teams (FDT) to optimize core accounting processes, leveraging automation tools (such as Workday Accounting Center and Workiva) to drive a low-touch, continuous close;

• Partner with Tax and FinOps teams to maintain a scalable intercompany framework and review reconciliations;

• Act as the single point of contact (SPOC) for Group External Auditors. Lead audit readiness, manage group audit deliverables, and take a leading role in our audit firm rotation;

• Own the monthly consolidated P&amp;L one pager (Net Revenue and EBITDA), explaining variances between actuals and the set expectation with clear business context and building the validation tools needed to produce it;

• Review and approve balance sheet reconciliations;&nbsp;

• Own month-end close activities,coordination and setting of consolidated and regional materiality thresholds;

• Continuously upskill others (GL accountants &amp; other Controllers) on core processes to build a shared understanding of end-to-end horizontal processes.

Who you are

• Minimum of 5+ years experience in financial control, accounting, or external audit (Big 4 experience is a strong plus);

• You have an analytical mindset and proactively identify challenges and be able to work independently but never afraid to ask for help;

• Experience managing complex multi-entity global accounting, intercompany settlements, cross-border flows, and transfer pricing;

• Strong IFRS knowledge, experience managing complex external audits;

• Track record in process optimization and automation. Experience with Workday, Workday Accounting Center, Workiva, or similar ERP systems is a plus;

• Ability to work on multiple projects simultaneously; ability to prioritise;

• Able to think 2 steps ahead. We are looking for someone that can think critically and creatively to implement solutions to scale during Adyen’s rapid growth.

Our Diversity, Equity and Inclusion commitments&nbsp;

Our unique approach is a product of our diverse perspectives. This diversity of backgrounds and cultures is essential in helping us maintain our momentum. Our business and technical challenges are unique, and we need as many different voices as possible to join us in solving them - voices like yours. No matter who you are or where you’re from, we welcome you to be your true self at Adyen.&nbsp;

